    {
      "id": "handle-invariants",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Invariants",
      "position": {
        "x": 1130,
        "y": -1536
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Invariants",
        "body": "- A Handle changes how a Port looks and nothing about how it behaves. Dragging, dropping and the rules for what may connect are the same with or without one.\n- The Port's own Handle wins over the root's default.\n- The root's default reaches the Ports its graph exposes and the root's own handles. It does not reach ordinary nodes inside the graph.\n- A Handle that cannot be reached is not an error: the Port is drawn as the plain disc.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592070377,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
